.\" vi: set sw=4 ts=4:
.TH MY_PROC 1 "2026-05-11" "BusyBox Diagnostic Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
my_proc \- interactive process viewer and system resource analyzer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B my_proc
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B my_proc
provides real-time system process monitoring with support for both list and
hierarchical tree views. It displays CPU usage, memory consumption (RSS/VSZ),
process states, and execution time, featuring dynamic sorting and an interactive
user interface.
.PP
Core features:
.IP \(bu 2
Real-time Monitoring: Automatically refreshes process lists and CPU/Memory statistics.
.IP \(bu 2
Tree View: Builds a process tree based on PPID relationships to visualize parent-child hierarchies.
.IP \(bu 2
Multi-dimensional Sorting: Supports sorting by CPU, Memory, PID, User, State, and Command.
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive Operations: Dynamically switch views, change sort modes, or send signals to terminate processes during runtime.
.IP \(bu 2
Batch Mode: Supports non-interactive output, suitable for logging or scripting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Tree view mode. Starts the application with the hierarchical process tree display.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Delay time between updates. Default is 1.0 second.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR \fICOUNT\fR
Number of iterations. Exit after updating the specified number of times.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR \fIPID\fR
Monitor a specific PID. Only displays information related to the target process.
.TP
.B \-b
Batch mode. Disables terminal control sequences and ignores keyboard input, ideal for redirection to files.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
In non-batch mode, the following keys are supported:
.TP
.B T
Toggle between List view (TOP) and Tree view (TREE).
.TP
.B Q
Quit the program.
.TP
.B K
Kill process. Prompts for a PID to send the SIGTERM signal.
.TP
.B Sorting Control
Press any of the following characters to sort the list:
.RS
.IP \fBP\fR 8
Sort by CPU usage percentage (Default)
.IP \fBM\fR 8
Sort by RSS (Resident Set Size)
.IP \fBV\fR 8
Sort by VSZ (Virtual Memory Size)
.IP \fBI\fR 8
Sort by PID (Process ID)
.IP \fBO\fR 8
Sort by PPID (Parent Process ID)
.IP \fBU\fR 8
Sort by USER (Username)
.IP \fBS\fR 8
Sort by STAT (Process State)
.IP \fBC\fR 8
Sort by COMMAND (Command name)
.RE
.SH COLUMNS
.TP
.B PID
Process Identification number.
.TP
.B PPID
Parent Process Identification number.
.TP
.B THR
Number of threads.
.TP
.B USER
Username of the process owner.
.TP
.B STAT
Process state (R: Running, S: Sleeping, D: Uninterruptible sleep, Z: Zombie, T: Stopped).
.TP
.B NI
Nice value (Scheduling priority).
.TP
.B VSZ
Total virtual memory size.
.TP
.B RSS
Resident Set Size (Physical memory currently used).
.TP
.B %CPU
CPU usage percentage since the last update.
.TP
.B %MEM
Physical memory usage percentage.
.TP
.B TIME
Total CPU time consumed by the process.
.TP
.B COMMAND
Command name .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure or insufficient permissions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR ps (1),
.BR pstree (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR proc (5)
